# `frontend/src/lib/api/` — typed API client (v2)

Typed fetch wrappers for the Excelsior backend. UI never calls `fetch` directly — it
imports the helpers here, and components consume them through TanStack Query.

## `client.ts` — the shared transport

- `apiRequest<T>(path, opts)` and the `api.get/post/put/del` shorthands are the **only**
  place network requests originate.
- The default sends `credentials: 'include'` so the session cookie from `/api/auth/*` login
  flows to every `/api/v1` call. `createApiClient` gives a separate host an explicit API origin,
  player header provider, credential policy, and single-flight renewal callback. Credentials
  are configured per transport, not per call; service secrets remain in server adapters.
- **Unwraps the v1 envelope** `{ data, success, errors, meta }` and returns `.data`. Pass
  `{ raw: true }` to get the whole envelope (used for legacy endpoints / when you need
  `meta`).
- Throws **`ApiError`** (`message`, `status`, `code?`, `data?`) on non-2xx. `ApiError.data`
  carries the envelope `data` on errors (e.g. structured `validationErrors` from deck save).
  Catch `ApiError` to branch on `status`/`code`; never assume a thrown value is an `Error`
  string.
- `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` is on: never assign explicit `undefined` to optional fields
  (the client guards `code`/`data`/`body`/`signal` for this reason).

## Endpoint modules

`auth.ts`, `account.ts`, `decks.ts`, `collection.ts`, `catalog.ts`, `favorites.ts`,
`recent-updates.ts`. Each exports small async functions returning typed values from
`types.ts`. Targets:
- Data: **`/api/v1/*`** (Bearer-less, session-cookie auth in browser).
- Auth/session: legacy **`/api/auth/*`** (login, signup, guest, Google, logout, me).

## React Query key catalog (keep keys consistent for cache hits + invalidation)

- `['auth','me']`, `['app-config']` — current user + CDN/pool config (`AuthProvider`).
- `['catalog', <type|slug|tab>]`, `['sets']`, `['dbv-sets']`, `['foil-card-map']` — card data.
- `['deck', deckId]` — single deck detail.
- `['decks']` (umbrella), `['decks','mine',userId]`, `['decks','favorites',userId]`,
  `['decks','community']`, `['decks','tournament']` — deck lists.
- `['collection','me']`, `['recent-updates']`.

After any mutation, invalidate the **umbrella** key (`invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['decks'] })`)
or the specific subtree, matching the existing call sites. QueryClient defaults
(`main.tsx`): `retry: 1`, `refetchOnWindowFocus: false`, `staleTime: 5m`. Use a longer
`staleTime` for rarely-changing data (sets, config) as the existing queries do.

## Rules

- New endpoints: add a typed function in the matching module + its types in `types.ts`; do
  not inline `fetch`/paths in components.
- When the legacy/v1 HTTP contract changes, update `API_DOCUMENTATION.md` (legacy) or
  `API_V1.md` (v1) per the repo rules.
